{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Accept all valid biometric EU/EEA/CH national identity cards for entry to the UK",
        "additional_details": "Since 1 October 2021, it has been reported that the UK has suffered an enormous fall in inbound tourism from EU/EEA/CH citizens who have identity cards but not passports. Council Regulation (EU) 2025/1208 requires identity cards issued since 2 August 2021 to conform to a common format specified by ICAO Document 9303, including a biometric chip and machine-readable zone, making them secure and compatible with e-gates. The Home Office says it costs an estimated 75p more to process an entry to the UK at a desk compared to an e-gate.",
        "background": "On 1 October 2021, the UK ceased accepting visitors' EU/EEA/CH national identity cards for UK entry, even very secure biometric cards. We want to reverse this decision & configure the UK's passport e-gates & the ETA system to accept all biometric EU/EEA/CH national identity cards and passport cards",
